          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "چٹنی (chaṭnī) is usually tied to chāṭnā, \"to lick\". CDIAL lists that verb, and chaṭnā, \"to be tasted\", made from it, under a reconstructed caṭṭ, \"lick, taste\" (CDIAL 4573), but it does not list chaṭnī itself. English took the word as chutney."
            }
          ]
        },
